OpenAI's Ashoka Rajendra, who cofounded Orchestra Bio, on the prospect of a one-person biotech company:

"Whether you are in manufacturing, at a pharma company, in clinical operations, in discovery and so on, how can these systems help you do the existing work you're doing faster and at higher quality, explore wider space?"

"I think that's a rising tide that will lift the entire industry. There are some substantial constraints, right? Human biology only moves so quickly. Regulation is a big lever that needs to be changed."

"But the industry has seen... what can small teams do in order to make breakthrough medicines. And I do think this is a great amplifier for the whole industry, with some fundamental limits, of course, in biology."

@JayRughani: "Do you think we'll see one-person biotechs anytime soon?"

@ashokaraj_: "Very much so, yes."

